{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvKnqYvaWhbrhrQestEr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Chat agent now answers each message with an LLM reply instead of echoing it. None of this has been run: the new packages aren't installed and I couldn't look up current versions on npm.\n\n**What changed:**\n- **`src/index.js`**: `onMessage` turns the message into text and calls `generateText` with `createWorkersAI({ binding: this.env.AI })` using `@cf/meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct-fp8-fast`. It sends the resulting `text` back on the connection. If the call fails, it logs the error and sends a short \"something went wrong\" message so the client isn't left waiting.\n- **`package.json`**: added `\"ai\": \"^6.0.0\"` and `\"workers-ai-provider\": \"^3.0.0\"`.\n- **`wrangler.jsonc`**: added `\"ai\": { \"binding\": \"AI\" }`.\n\n**Check the versions when you install:** I picked `ai@^6` because the installed `agents` 0.27.0 accepts `ai` `^6.0.0 || ^7.0.0`, and I expect `workers-ai-provider@^3` to work with `ai` v6. I couldn't confirm that, so if npm reports a peer-dependency conflict, run `npm view workers-ai-provider peerDependencies` and adjust. If the latest provider supports `ai` v7, you can move both packages up to the latest versions.\n\nYour `compatibility_date` is 2026-10-01, so `nodejs_compat` is on by default with this Wrangler version and you don't need to add the flag. The AI binding uses Workers AI on your account even during `wrangler dev`, so it counts toward your usage."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1381,"cache_read_input_tokens":28220,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1381},"output_tokens":542,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"sessi